# Repo-local pins and build products — never tracked.
#
# .devenv-toolchain is the gcroot for the pinned devenv the machines work needs
# (2.4+ for `machines`; the global profile binary on a workstation is 2.2.2).
# Rebuild it with the command in bin/devenv's header.
.devenv-toolchain
.devenv/
.direnv/
result
result-*
# Issue tracker: local markdown tickets live here, per docs/agents/issue-tracker.md.
.scratch
# The nixos-facter report `devenv machines install` writes. The Machine sets
# hardware.facter = null and does not consume it, so this is a local record of
# the measured hardware, not config. Tracking it would make a later switch to
# the default facter path silently import a stale report.
.machines/

# DeepSeek Harness runtime home: sessions, settings imports, launch tokens,
# and operator credentials stay under the repo's dsh/ boundary, never tracked.
/dsh/.dsh/

# Hermes Agent runtime home (ticket 04 / hermes-config effort). The
# declarative `config.yaml` lives at `~/nix/hermes/.hermes/config.yaml`
# and IS tracked — it is the rendered source, not a secret. The OAuth
# token file and the API-key env file are NOT; both are populated by the
# upstream module's activation step (`authFile` first-write-wins,
# `environmentFiles` overwriting each activation). The `mcp-tokens/`
# directory holds per-server OAuth tokens written by the upstream
# hermes-agent runtime, also non-shareable.
#
# The runtime home does not exist yet (the cutover is ticket 08) — these
# patterns are written now so the entries are in place when the directory
# is created. `git status --porcelain` must continue to print nothing
# inside `~/nix/hermes/.hermes/` once it exists.
#
# Patterns are repo-root-relative (gitignore `/` means "from repo root").
/hermes/.hermes/auth.json
/hermes/.hermes/.env
/hermes/.hermes/.env.local
/hermes/.hermes/mcp-tokens/
